From 6a98efc580e149f70f15ec470e4db86db719c65b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 20:58:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Set the measured optimum as the default non-negativity weight

The sweep added in the previous commit measures lambda_nonneg = 10 as the
optimum, against the 1 that was the default. The error falls
monotonically from 1 to 10 and rises again after it (rel err fODF 0.105
at 10, 0.133 at 30, 0.417 at 100), so this is an interior optimum rather
than a grid edge. Against the previous default the relative fODF error
drops from 0.199 to 0.105 and the negative mass from 0.031 to 0.004,
which is the negative mass of the ground truth fODF itself.

Only the default weight changes. flag_nonneg and lambda_tikhonov still
default to 0, so a fit that does not set options.fODF_regularization is
bit-identical to before (verified, difference exactly 0), and the change
only reaches a user who enables the constraint without choosing a
weight.

tau = 0.1 and Lmax_init = 4 are confirmed as interior optima by the same
sweep and are unchanged. The Tikhonov matrix default stays 'identity'
even though Laplace-Beltrami scores 2.5% better once its weight is
re-optimized: the two differ by the max(l(l+1)) normalization, so
switching the default would silently rescale what any given
lambda_tikhonov means.

example_fODF_regularization.m enables the constraint without naming a
weight, so it picks up the new default; its relative fODF error goes
from 0.192 to 0.104 and the README figures are updated to match.

REPORT_fODF_regularization_sweep.md documents the simulation setup, the
parameters tested, every result table, the recommended versus original
settings, and the limitations of the experiment.

